# Line endings are part of the source. Without this, a Windows checkout (git's default
# core.autocrlf=true) turns every .sh into CRLF, which bash rejects ("$'\r': command not found"),
# and turns data and docs into CRLF too, which breaks byte-exact comparisons.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
